    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "With this effect, your opponent's memory will no longer increase by any effects except Tamer effects. This effect affects the opponent player.",
        "question": "What does the \"your opponent can't gain memory other than by Tamer effects\" effect do, exactly?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can gain memory.  When an effect is activated on a card that's treated as both a Digimon and a Tamer, the effect is treated as both a Digimon effect and a Tamer effect, therefore you can gain memory.",
        "question": "Can I use the [All Turns] effect on BT17-087 [Marcus Damon] to gain memory if it's treated as a Digimon and suspends while my opponent has \"your opponent can't gain memory other than by Tamer effects\" activated?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
